---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageFrame from "@components/PageFrame.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy – VISUA1HUE" description="What this site does and doesn't do with your data." noindex router>
  <PageFrame current="privacy">
    <article class="policy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
      <header class="policy-head">
        <h1 class="page-title" id="privacy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-15">15 November 2026</time></p>
      </header>
      {/* TODO before launch: "No cookies" holds only while no Cloudflare bot feature sets one (Security → Bots) */}
      {/* Links start on the text's line ("See <a"): compressHTML drops a line break before an inline element */}

      <p class="lead">
        <strong>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking.</strong> This site doesn't load anything from third parties: fonts
        and scripts are served from this domain.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <address>Michael Hübel<br />privacy [at] visua1hue.dev</address>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site runs on Cloudflare. To deliver and protect it, Cloudflare processes technical data for every request:
        IP address, browser, requested page and time.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Why:</strong> to deliver the site and keep it secure, including blocking attack traffic.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. My legitimate interest is a site that loads and is protected
          against misuse.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Who receives it:</strong> Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. Cloudflare
          processes this data on my behalf under a data processing agreement. For some data, such as data used to secure
          its own network, Cloudflare acts on its own responsibility. See <a
            href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Outside the EU:</strong> Cloudflare may process the data in the USA and other countries. Cloudflare is
          certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, which the European Commission has found adequate (Art. 45
          GDPR). Its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/">data processing agreement</a> also
          includes the EU Standard Contractual Clauses (Art. 46 GDPR).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Error logs:</strong> Cloudflare keeps request logs for this site in my account. I use them only to find
          and fix errors. They are deleted after 3 days.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How long:</strong> apart from those logs, I keep no logs of my own. Cloudflare shows me aggregated
          traffic and security statistics for about a month. Cloudflare deletes its own records once it no longer needs
          them for delivery and security; it doesn't publish fixed periods.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Page preloading</h2>
      <p>
        To make page changes faster, your browser may load the other page of this site in advance. These requests only go
        to this domain and are handled as described under Hosting.
      </p>

      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>Fonts are hosted on this domain. Your browser doesn't contact Google or any other font provider.</p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email an address at visua1hue.dev, Cloudflare forwards your message to my private inbox at my email
        provider. I use your address and message only to reply, and delete them once the conversation is finished. Legal
        basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my interest in answering your message.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Links to LinkedIn, GitHub and Centric Software are plain links. Nothing is sent to them until you click. After
        that, their privacy policies apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Do you have to provide data?</h2>
      <p>
        No law or contract requires it. Without your IP address and request data, your browser can't load the site. There
        is no automated decision-making or profiling (Art. 22 GDPR).
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask for access to your data (Art. 15 GDPR), correction (Art. 16), deletion (Art. 17) and restriction of
        processing (Art. 18). Write to privacy [at] visua1hue.dev. I usually can't link request data to a person, so I may
        ask for details that help me find yours (Art. 11 GDPR).
      </p>

      <h2>Right to object</h2>
      <p>
        You can object at any time, on grounds relating to your situation, to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (Art.
        21 GDPR). I will then stop unless I can show compelling legitimate grounds that override your interests, or the
        processing is needed for legal claims.
      </p>

      <h2>Right to complain</h2>
      <p>
        You can complain to a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR), in particular in the EU country where
        you live or work or where you think the violation happened. German authorities are listed by the <a
          href="https://www.datenschutzkonferenz-online.de/datenschutzaufsichtsbehoerden.html">Datenschutzkonferenz</a
        >.
      </p>
    </article>
  </PageFrame>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 680px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
  }

  /* Date sits right of the title, baseline-aligned; wraps under it when the row is too narrow */
  .policy-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 4px 24px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.32;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    color: var(--color-subtle);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 48px 0 10px;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-fg);
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  address {
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--color-subtle);
  }

  ul {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  strong {
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    color: var(--color-fg);
  }

  p a,
  li a {
    color: var(--color-fg);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
</style>
